<% content_for :title, "Average Return Calculator — whizwheel" %>

<%#
  Average Return calculator page (spec issue #257, DESIGN.md BLEND). A VARIABLE-LENGTH
  LIST input — a series of period returns (each a percent) — posted as `inputs[returns][]`
  (the array attribute the backend permits via Base.array_attribute, ARCHITECTURE.md §3.2).
  Unlike Mean·Median·Mode·Range's comma-string textarea, this list is a DYNAMIC ADD/REMOVE
  set of individual fields: a `return_list` Stimulus controller grows/shrinks the list and
  keeps a live period count. There is NO mode picker — both averages are always reported.

  Progressive enhancement (DESIGN.md §0.5): the page server-renders a few starter
  `inputs[returns][]` rows, and the server owns the list parse (it drops blanks and validates
  ≥ 1 remains) — so the dynamic UI is a layer of polish, not a gate on the data. Stimulus ADDS
  the Add/Remove buttons, row focus, and the live count chip over those starter rows. It posts
  over Turbo (like the rest of the catalog) and re-renders #result in place.

  After a 422 the form re-renders the SUBMITTED returns (average_return_rows), so the user
  keeps what they typed. Layout per DESIGN.md §3 — input column + results panel (≈380px 1fr),
  one stacked column on mobile.

  The row markup is generated by one helper (#return_row) shared between the server-rendered
  starter rows and the Stimulus <template> (the JS clone source), so a cloned row is byte-
  identical to a server-rendered one — no duplicated row HTML (DESIGN.md §5 guardrail).
%>

<% rows = average_return_rows(@calc) %>

<header class="max-w-2xl">
  <p class="text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-accent">Financial</p>
  <h1 class="mt-2 text-4xl font-extrabold tracking-[-0.035em] text-ink">Average Return Calculator</h1>
  <p class="mt-3 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-muted">
    Enter a series of period returns (each a percent) and get both averages — the simple
    <span class="font-semibold text-ink">arithmetic average</span> and the compounded
    <span class="font-semibold text-ink">geometric average</span>, the financially meaningful
    "true" rate that accounts for compounding. A loss is a negative return (e.g.
    <span class="font-semibold text-ink">−5</span>). Every answer is computed server-side.
  </p>
</header>

<div class="mt-8 grid grid-cols-1 gap-8 lg:grid-cols-[380px_1fr]">
  <%# ── Input column ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────── %>
  <section class="rounded-[18px] border border-border bg-surface p-7 shadow-[0_10px_34px_rgba(150,110,80,0.12)] sm:p-8">
    <%= form_with url: "/calculators/average_return", scope: :inputs, method: :post,
          data: { controller: "return-list" } do |f| %>

      <div class="flex items-end justify-between gap-3">
        <div>
          <span class="field-label" id="returns_label">Period returns</span>
          <p id="returns_hint" class="mt-1 text-xs leading-relaxed text-muted">
            One per period, as a percent — e.g. <span class="font-semibold text-ink">10</span>,
            <span class="font-semibold text-ink">20</span>, <span class="font-semibold text-ink">−5</span>.
          </p>
        </div>
        <%# Live period-count chip — updated by the controller as rows are added/removed. %>
        <span data-return-list-target="count"
              class="shrink-0 rounded-full bg-accent/10 px-3 py-1 text-xs font-bold tabular-nums text-accent">
          <%= rows.size == 1 ? "1 period" : "#{rows.size} periods" %>
        </span>
      </div>

      <%# The list of return rows — the Turbo/Stimulus list region. Each row is one
          `inputs[returns][]` field with a leading "Period n" label and a remove button.
          Stacked tier (DESIGN.md §3, space-y-3 — rows are tightly related siblings). %>
      <div role="group" aria-labelledby="returns_label" aria-describedby="returns_hint"
           data-return-list-target="list" class="mt-3 space-y-3">
        <% rows.each do |value| %>
          <%= render "calculators/average_return_row", value: value %>
        <% end %>
      </div>

      <%# The clone source for the Stimulus controller — an empty row, rendered identically
          to a server row. Inert until JS clones it (its inputs don't post — a <template>'s
          content is not part of the document). %>
      <template data-return-list-target="template">
        <%= render "calculators/average_return_row", value: "" %>
      </template>

      <%# Add another period — a quiet secondary affordance (the "today-button" vocabulary:
          outlined chip, warms to accent on hover), distinct from the coral primary submit.
          A real <button type="button"> so it never submits the form; the Stimulus controller
          clones a fresh row on tap. (Like the rest of the catalog, the page is enhanced by
          Turbo + Stimulus; the starter rows + server-side list parse are the graceful floor.) %>
      <button type="button" data-action="return-list#add"
              class="today-button mt-4 flex w-full items-center justify-center gap-2">
        <span aria-hidden="true" class="text-base leading-none">+</span> Add return
      </button>

      <%# Submit — Section tier above; primary coral button (DESIGN.md §4). %>
      <%= f.submit "Calculate",
            class: "mt-8 w-full cursor-pointer rounded-[13px] bg-primary px-4 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-surface shadow-sm transition-opacity hover:opacity-90 focus:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-accent" %>
    <% end %>
  </section>

  <%# ── Results panel (the Turbo target) ─────────────────────────────────── %>
  <section id="result" aria-live="polite">
    <%= render "calculators/result", calc: nil %>
  </section>
</div>
